{
  "name": "Event Request Alert by Zipcode - Demo",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Event Request Alert by ZIP Code\n\n\nWhat?\n\nThis workflow identifies when enough people in the same ZIP-code area request a future n8n community event.\n\n\nHow?\n\nA user submits a short form with their name, email, ZIP code, preferred event type, and optional topic.\n\nThe workflow saves the request in Google Sheets, reads all requests, removes duplicate submissions for the same email and ZIP code, and groups demand by ZIP-code prefix.\n\nWhen 5 or more unique people request an event in the same ZIP-code area, the workflow sends a Slack alert to the marketing/community team.\n\n\nNext steps:\n- The team decides whether to plan a meetup, workshop, hack night, or live build session.\n- If an event is organized in that area, users who requested it can automatically be notified.\n- Future versions could add true radius mapping, ambassador matching, Notion/Jira follow-up, and a data dashboard.\n\n",
        "height": 672,
        "width": 432
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
